A||||10||sluppy123||Better Ignition Module||||5||
Z||000000||sluppy123||03-14-2000||07:48 PM||||Anybody know of a better ignition module that might last a little longer than the cheap foreign aftermarket one's????  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>-Brian||||reg||5
Z||000001||AL||03-14-2000||09:00 PM||||GM original products always lasts better!||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIEROCIOUS||03-15-2000||01:12 AM||||Accel makes one! Go to your local PepBoys!<BR>They'll have to order it but it is available.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FieroGTRacingInc||03-15-2000||07:49 AM||||Is the Accel module better than the GM module???||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||03-15-2000||11:45 AM||||Blue Streak, MSD, Accel, and AC Delco. all make units for our cars. (V6). I've used the Accel, Blue Streak and MSD ones.. all cost about the same as the DELCO one and can't really tell a difference in any of them. other than The BlueStreak one doesn't seal up well with the factory plugs and DIES when it get wet...  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||03-15-2000||07:13 PM||||I won't buy blue freak unless it absolutly the only thing I can get and then I have to be near death.<P>Borg Warner has these as well I think. You can get them on wrenchead.com, maybe carparts.com.<P>Always use fresh heatsink compound when installing these. You can get it a radio shack and most other electronics suppliers. The regular "dielectric grease" is not as good, but better than nothing. (Thermaloy, one maker of heatsinks, rates the white compound 4 times better than plain dielectric grease, and 20 times better than nothing.)||||reg||1
Z||000006||sluppy123||03-15-2000||08:52 PM||||Anybody have a part # for the Accel or MSD module? thanks<BR>-Brain<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Earne||03-15-2000||11:34 PM||||MSD Blaster GM Coil, PN 8226<P>For increased ignition performance, MSD suggests an MSD Ignition Control installed with a PN 8876 Harness for a direct plug-in installation.||||reg||1
Z||000008||geyser||03-16-2000||01:14 AM||||If you are looking for an MSD ignition module, you have some choices- #6 or 6AL (I have the 6AL) are good choices. Both perform the same, the 6AL includes an adjustable rev limiter system  that can also serve to activate switches or solenoids at a selected rpm. I am going to use mine to activate a nitrous solenoid and an ignition retard system. Don't expect really noticable performance increases, the stock system is really very good. Also the numbers Erne gave you are correct for the addition of an MSD coil and the plug in harness that will make the installation of thr module much cleaner.  ||||reg||6
Z||000009||FIEROCIOUS||03-16-2000||01:27 AM||||I'll get that P/N for ya ASAP MSD's and Accel's. Slupps is talking about the module inside the distributor! not an capacitive discharge ignition.<BR>P.S. the modules can be used with the CD ignitions.||||reg||1
Z||000010||WKDFIRO||03-17-2000||12:53 AM||||Blue Freak! Now thats funny!<P>I agree 100% with Al. GM/AC Delco parts for me!||||reg||14
